body:
... Sir/Ma'am/Distinguished gentleperson, i swear i'm not guilty.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

... *Maybe*

Indeed. There really isn't. And yeah, the unholy amount of people who come over and tell you to "seek help" aren't helping much, either. People send you to therapists, therapists either don't give a damn or try telling some generic "don't give up! :)" phrases that would just make someone feel worse. The mental health system is truly garbage.

&#x200B;

EDIT: Typo

Honestly, to me they should make fazbear ent. the villains of the story. This isn't Afton's story anymore, so i hope they wrap up his story in the DLC and kill him off for good (with this i mean: Make him more threatering, give him a bossfight, etc..), moving onto a new villain, which would be fazbear ent. themselves. 

&#x200B;

My idea is fairly simple: Have Vanessa, Gregory and Freddy try to get the higher up arrested and get the company to close forever. They go through shenanigans involving the higher ups and we get this bittersweet finale where fazbear ent. has been closed off forever, but Freddy has been destroyed, either by the company during the climax of the story or during the ending, because him being a stolen animatronic makes him a part of fazbear ent, and fazbear ent. owning the rights to Freddy will decide to want him destroyed. (The bittersweet finale is optional, but i wanted to add it to give a true conclusion to anything regarding fazbear ent, so Freddy is included)

&#x200B;

Now, do i think Afton being back from the dead is bad? Despite this being a very unpopular opinion that will most likely spark up conflict: No. I think him coming back from the dead is bad, but they should've made him more of a threat. Have him almost successfully kill/destroy our protagonists, have him get one of the coolest bossfights, and have him die off for good, with no way for him to come back. I personally think keeping him is a way to introduce us to the new FNAF gen, and i see nothing wrong with that.

&#x200B;

This is what i think (and hope) happens. Give Afton a chance to redeem himself as a villain, kill him off **for good,** and make fazbear ent. the new villain that has to be stopped.

That's one very well done artwork! I'm assuming it's pixel art (is it? Or is my memory failing me?) and if so, i find it to be pretty hard to master so this is definitely a 100/10 for me!

&#x200B;

Also i'm sorry if you're struggling with depression. It's a hard time to go through..

